    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24ZXU9uTRrMUi2hdxaUsWPV)_\n\nFollow-up to #196, which is merged.\n\n- You asked for the `vulpea-graph` block in the tangled `sp-graphs.el` and for `docker-compose-mode` to be removed from `sp-prog-misc`. Both already hold on `main`: `sp-graphs.el` has the block and nothing mentions `docker-compose-mode` any more (your re-tangle commits fixed them), so those two entries are gone from `tools/tangle-drift-allow.txt`.\n- The check found one new difference on `main`: the `sp-fetch-academic` doc has a `litdb` `use-package` block its `.el` lacks. Same rule as `vulpea-graph` (the doc is the source), so I added the block to the `.el` by hand, in the exact form the tangle writes it.\n- `tools/tangle-drift-allow.txt` is now empty; the docs say so.\n\nTested in Emacs 29.3 in batch: `tools/check-tangle.sh` reports that all tangled modules match their docs. The GitHub run is the first check on this change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCnPfpYNzCoPgTiWqZ)_",
